    "field": "Flood risk assessment",
    "problem": "Flood risk assessment methodologies, applications, and uncertainties differ notably across various spatial scales, creating challenges for model improvement, validation, and the linking of assessments between scales, which this review aims to explore and address.",
    "method": "This review paper compares flood risk assessment methodologies across four spatial scales (supra-national, macro, meso, micro), examining differences in their approaches to hazard estimation, consequence analysis, uncertainty, and validation to identify key characteristics and research needs for each scale.",
    "task": "The task is to review and compare the methodologies, uses, and uncertainties of quantitative flood risk assessments across different spatial scales, from global to local, to identify differences and future research needs.",
